The shallow water equations on sparse tiles (benchmarks/swe/swe-sparse.m)
in a GPU process on the machine's GPU: a team steps each active tile, its
threads over the tile's cells, and the process's lane does the
bookkeeping. Every output is swe-sparse.c's at the host, bit for bit
(swe-sparse.test), the default world too, 2048 cells square in tiles of
32, where the water covers 472 tiles after 1000 steps.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/swe/swe-sparse.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env SWE_WORLD=256 SWE_TILE=16 SWE_STEPS=400 SWE_CASE=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %S/swe-sparse.test --check-prefix=THACKER --match-full-lines
RUN: %gpu-env SWE_WORLD=256 SWE_TILE=16 SWE_STEPS=400 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %S/swe-sparse.test --check-prefix=COLUMN --match-full-lines
RUN: %gpu-env SWE_WORLD=512 SWE_TILE=64 SWE_STEPS=200 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %S/swe-sparse.test --check-prefix=WIDE --match-full-lines
RUN: %gpu-env SWE_WORLD=64 SWE_TILE=4 SWE_STEPS=300 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %S/swe-sparse.test --check-prefix=SMALL --match-full-lines
RUN: %gpu-env timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEFAULT --match-full-lines
DEFAULT: World: 2048 x 2048 cells, tiles of 32 x 32, 4096 in the pool
DEFAULT: Time: 24.536581448 s
DEFAULT-NEXT: Wet cells: 428060
DEFAULT-NEXT: Volume: 2.524112e+05 m^3
DEFAULT-NEXT: Checksum: 55015ede6d1e4270
DEFAULT-NEXT: Active tiles: 472 at most, 472 at the end
RUN: %gpu-env SWE_WORLD=256 SWE_TILE=16 SWE_STEPS=400 SWE_CAPACITY=40 not timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %S/swe-sparse.test --check-prefix=FULL

Without -fopenmp the process runs the loops on its own lane.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/swe/swe-sparse.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: %gpu-env SWE_WORLD=64 SWE_TILE=4 SWE_STEPS=300 timeout -k 1 60 %t.sequential | FileCheck %S/swe-sparse.test --check-prefix=SMALL --match-full-lines
